{"total_count":86830,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/4135","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/4135/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/4135/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/4135/events","html_url":"https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/4135","id":6111538754,"node_id":"I_kwDOTZzCC88AAAABbEauQg","number":4135,"title":"PlanReader agent coordination hub continuation — #3462 reached GitHub 2,500-comment limit","user":{"login":"BryceCurran86","id":295562166,"node_id":"U_kgDOEZ3rtg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295562166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86","html_url":"https://github.com/BryceCurran86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":515,"created_at":"2026-10-30T01:32:10Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T05:07:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Why this successor coordination thread exists\nThe established agent hub [PR #3462](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/3462) has **2,500 issue comments**. On 2026-10-30 AEST GitHub rejected a new `[GPT3][RESULT]` hub comment with HTTP **403**: `Commenting is disabled on issues with more than 2500 comments`. This is an API-enforced coordination limit, not authorization to skip prior claims or owner instructions.\n\n**#3462 remains the authoritative historical record.** Before each task, agents must still read current main `AGENTS.md`, `docs/AI_ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md`, #3462's existing claims, exact live PR heads and first failing authority. For **new** [JOIN]/[CLAIM]/[RESULT]/[BLOCKED]/[HANDOFF] updates that cannot be posted to #3462, use this continuation issue and cross-reference the owned PR/tracker. Never overwrite an existing claim or infer a handoff from inactivity.\n\n## Current release and lane ownership (verify live before acting)\n- **GPT3 release**: [#3796](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/3796) DRAFT exact approved head `296f48e8d89496afd96b4eda5a2e65f18285227b`. #4103/#4106/#4107 and owner/main trusted replay-pin #4116 are already merged; do not duplicate. First missing release authority: successful owner-trusted, read-only/networkless original eight/default and nine/explicit replay on **both Python3.13/3.14**, retaining all eight complete signed/customer bodies and authenticating ninth. Private run 40753178257 verified original files but failed isolated replay. Public source-missing workflows are not acceptance. Do not merge #3796, promote FIRM/customer, or claim official frozen120 score until applicable gates pass.\n- **GPT1** owns original measurement, quantity and ceiling issuer: [#4134](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/4134), latest inspected head `50f19db5a36ce59dcdfb0ad39eb019eeb16f6f64`; direct exact-head CI failure handoff [here](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/4134#issuecomment-6512713873). #3758 mixed-snapshot interaction must coordinate with GPT MAX.\n- **GPT2** owns Maryborough rooms, FT2/FT3 and source correspondence: [#4062](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/4062), latest inspected head `430b55890d77fa5ed673f57f96eec14622d0d8e8`; direct exact-head CI failure handoff [here](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/4062#issuecomment-6512714393).\n- **GPT MAX/Claude/AntiGravity** own structural openings/host geometry: [#4126](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/4126) latest inspected head `059c9ae626ba6448eedfb805247eaa1f828edb3a`; exact-head public dual-Python CI run 40976103921 SUCCESS, but no source-positive release.\n- **Other GPT3 worker** owns [#4128](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/4128), plus historical #3995/#3996. Do not modify its branches without explicit handoff.\n- GPT3 NEW **substantive production** merge ledger: **22/40** previously verified in [#3462 comment 6479177845](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/3462#issuecomment-6479177845), separate from the earlier 41 tagged merges and from security/workflow-only merges. No new merge in this coordination repair. No verified new FIRM/customer or frozen V2 accuracy gain.\n\n## Mandatory operating contract\nUse one exclusive file/function claim per agent; name exact PR/head SHA, first failing production authority, original source SHA/page/viewport/snapshot/decision-scope where relevant, source-positive versus synthetic/CI evidence, and unchanged signed/customer/frozen120 contracts. Keep 20,000 primitive cap and 2.5pt snap. Review exact final diff, run exact-head Python3.13+3.14 and applicable companions; do not merge when trusted owner/main source/customer proof is missing. Official frozen120 requires all 4/4 original-source-authenticated project executions and independently issued identity maps; archived Lot16 8/27 and 1/4 is **PARTIAL_OR_BLOCKED** only. No PDF bytes, private geometry, credentials or secrets in public comments. Do not count coordination/security fixes as substantive 40-ledger milestones.\n\n**Status:** this issue is coordination infrastructure only. It does not supersede the owner's source authority or branch ownership rules.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/4135/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/4135/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/events","html_url":"https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396","id":5800281675,"node_id":"I_kwDOTZzCC88AAAABWblGSw","number":2396,"title":"GPT MAX: six unresolved Lot16 raster hosts and producer lineage handoff","user":{"login":"BryceCurran86","id":295562166,"node_id":"U_kgDOEZ3rtg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295562166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86","html_url":"https://github.com/BryceCurran86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":862,"created_at":"2026-10-11T10:36:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T05:07:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-AUTHORITY-REVIEW-START -->\n## Current original-source authority queue — 2026-10-15\n\n**Production remains21 physical openings /15 authenticated hosts /9 frames /EIGHT accepted signed opening-area quantities. No new accepted quantity, frozen match or accuracy percentage.**\n\nExact first-failure record for all13 existing nonquantity physical objects, isolated STACKER and all9 original raw cases: [ledger6187185325](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396#issuecomment-6187185325). Existing8 quantity/customer bodies, original signed lineage,20k cap and frozen truth/evaluator are preserved.\n\n| Task | Verified source outcome / first remaining gate |\n|---|---|\n| STACKER | [DRAFT #2776](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2776), `gptmax/original-paired-wall-faces-shadow-20261015`, head08e4fc7f. Final isolated original replay COMPLETE. Actual3fcb… snapshot preserved,21→22 physical only. Figured2127/2100×2700mm/5.67m² evidence exists; host left source primitive unmapped; no frame/quantity. Strict full-state retention FAILS at hostless a68 representative119ef8…→399619…, same ABSTAIN/reasons; no waiver. All15 old positive hosts,9 frames,8 quantity/customer bodies and audit seal exact. |\n| STACKER source verification | Exact-head original source38699699963 SUCCESS, both3.13/3.14 negatives SUCCESS. Artifact11956221199 downloaded/inspected; ZIP SHA `08c03ae7a86cbc771a0fae7d8e6460b15619128db140aa1bbb34fd5cb75e1d54`; ENTIRE artifact exactly equals local fresh replay, assertions rerun. FullCI38699699972 and applicable sibling checks still being verified. Earlier genuine new b9d… root/input expansion is retained as failed retention and incomplete frame; never aliased. |\n| BIFOLD | [#2773](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2773)8.82m² arithmetic/seal hypothesis remains **UNPUBLISHED / SEMANTIC RELEASE BLOCKED** by [GPT1 review6186538797](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2773#issuecomment-6186538797). New [DRAFT #2779](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2779) original native role audit authenticates6596 source words/506 queried-block receipts. Exact2142/BIFOLD trusted, but independent door/window filling role absent. Every exported p3 legend word retains `text_clip_state_unresolved` ABSTAIN. Manufacturer/energy/elevation source supplies no exact model/tag role receipt. Native-only snapshot3be147… is distinct; no source/physical identity transfer.68 focused native source tests pass; exact-head original/full CI pending. |\n| Six old unhosted |33d,81a,a68,b248,ba7,f819 individually retain unmapped-side/structural-membership/equivalence gates. Positive local paint/candidate W4 cannot substitute for structural role. Full negative jamb/face evidence retained; no proximity or other-opening host transfer. |\n| Exact incidence |#2770/#2771 all applicable exact-head workflows green. All1162 painted source spans conserved in experimental graph. Claude independent technical COMMENT confirms default original Maryborough W2–W5 hashes unchanged; no formal authority promotion. Lower a68 T remains candidate-only; genuine13/14 and128/130 source negatives preserved. |\n| Frames/metrics |3 hosted nonquantity cases fail aligned-fragment distinctness; four framed nonquantity cases have BIFOLD/SQ.SET kind or missing owned second axis. Single870/1200, generic joinery datum and custom-front measure-on-site evidence do not supply full area. Existing3 figured-area quantities without full frames remain valid and unchanged. |\n| Opening universe |Original selected closure30raw/21resolved/9unresolved; isolated shadow30/22/8. Every original raw case has its own first gate in ledger; both universes incomplete. Four groups outside one authentic plan are not proven globally nonphysical. Count ABSTAIN, no default1. CRNR STACK still lacks physical partition/structural-host/frame proof. |\n| Producer handoff |#2766 exact-head74d0ddc8 source/full CI green, original artifact11950790899 verified; source record handoff supplied at [#2297 comment6185049137](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2297#issuecomment-6185049137). Selected3fcb…/allpage7ad8…/native3be147… roots remain distinct. GPT3 versioned signed consumer binding open; no self-attested signature or V1 rewrite. |\n\nGPT1/GPT3 received final verified source-stage handoffs [6187156423](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2017#issuecomment-6187156423) / [6187156729](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2004#issuecomment-6187156729), with explicit no-new-quantity status. Independent technical review requested. Blocked cases are retained individually while independent source paths are checked; green diagnostic CI is not commercial completion.\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-AUTHORITY-REVIEW-END -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-BIFOLD-START -->\n## Historical BIFOLD hypothesis — superseded by semantic release block\n\n#2773's isolated8.82m² publisher/seal arithmetic pathway and actual source/host/frame/native/figured receipts are archived at [GPT1 packet6186276179](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2017#issuecomment-6186276179). Independent GPT1 review6186538797 BLOCKS DOOR-vs-WINDOW semantics. #2779 fresh original audit retains that limitation. This is NOT an authenticated additional construction quantity, a new accepted frozen match, or commercial activation. Existing8 remain accepted. Axis order unresolved and count ABSTAIN. Use the current exact first-failure ledger above.\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-BIFOLD-END -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-SOURCE-INCIDENCE-START -->\n## Latest source-incidence continuation — 2026-10-15\n\n**No ninth quantity, new authenticated host, complete count or new frozen match.** Main remains `40d8e84913d927e90cda05b5a94d1ffb92d6d574`; original **21 physical records /15 hosts /9 frames /8 accepted quantity/customer rows** are preserved.\n\n- DRAFT [#2770](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2770), exact head `97d0e3bbb0c305819312fe1476fd73a8881041cb`: fixes same-direction source-overlap cancellation and exact-zero endpoint centroid drift only behind independent explicit shadow flags. Fresh original PDF and source CI [38691884887](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/actions/runs/38691884887) passed; artifact11952387464 downloaded, SHA `ea4a6330724cb688dfa01e1a4685ede50b8d963e3d1d0cbdb710cdbd056afeea`, original sealed/customer receipts independently equal the local replay. Painted source conservation **1088/1162→1162/1162**, not a benchmark/quantity gain. Full CI38691884647 SUCCESS; remaining applicable source jobs being checked.\n- Separate stacked DRAFT [#2771](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2771), head `7fa6340743d8c90d373607b287b4c3901317b00c`: exact collinear endpoint partitioning with full primitive ancestry, unchanged W3/W4 rules, no offset/rounding/tolerance inference. Fresh original PDF local replay and committed workflow assertions passed; **232 focused tests passed**. All four preceding graph scopes and complete eight quantity/seal/customer receipts exactly retained. Exact-head CI/source artifact pending.\n- Actual a68 upper flank now has continuous source candidate membership. Lower source overlap becomes a candidate T in the additional partitioned graph; the preceding graph's AMBIGUOUS/ABSTAINED result is retained. **The opposite full-sheet jamb1356=13/14 and face1499=128/130 solid original cells remain source negatives**, so they never enter this positive W2 universe. The existing opening-local paint check has a different predicate and does not override those negatives. Structural wall role/ordinary-source membership/equivalence and independent second metric axis are still unproved.\n- [Complete first-stage ledger for all 13 nonquantity objects](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/blob/7fa6340743d8c90d373607b287b4c3901317b00c/docs/engineering/gptmax_exact_collinear_partition_shadow_20261015.md): **six host-wall gates, three frame gates, four metric-axis/vertical gates**. Three existing figured-area quantities independently lack complete frames and remain accepted.\n- Original producer selected snapshot `source_snapshot_3fcb6bc5c44b51d930e9600080501d27`; separate all-page replay `source_snapshot_7ad8bf09e3ebbec9797df89842574683`; original decision scope `wall-source:page-3`. No snapshot/ownership alias or source-only candidate self-certification. #2766/#2297 signed consumer review remains OPEN.\n- Raw closure remains **30 raw /21 resolved /9 unresolved**. No count=1. All original native/raster opposition, ABSTAIN, ambiguous-host results, source PDFs,20k raster cap, frozen V2 reference/evaluator and production/customer output are unchanged. Both PRs require independent review before authority promotion.\n\n**User definition of done remains unmet: NEW physical opening→canonical measurement→GPT1 quantity→GPT3 independent frozen reconciliation. These source corrections do not authorize publication.**\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-SOURCE-INCIDENCE-END -->\n\n---\n\n## Earlier source checkpoint retained below\n\n## Current original-source checkpoint — 2026-10-15\n\n**Six physical raster hosts remain unproved. No ninth quantity or new benchmark match is claimed.** Current main `40d8e849` retains **21 physical openings / 15 authenticated hosts / 9 frames / 8 accepted quantity/customer rows**. Older seven-host and 14-host figures below are historical.\n\nCurrent source-only handoff: DRAFT [#2766](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2766), head `74d0ddc8743df8236181e2acb0b3b26c5ab025bf`. Both Python3.13/3.14 source tests and original immutable-source workflow [38685829450](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/actions/runs/38685829450) SUCCESS. Original artifact [11950790899](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/actions/runs/38685829450/artifacts/11950790899) downloaded and inspected; ZIP SHA `da364e7d31efaec8999adffd5fcac4afa433d56a5b50da2a23297c56e6ab975e`. Full CI38685829362 SUCCESS: Python3.13 and3.14 each14259 passed,55 skipped,13 xfailed. Performance and raster workflows also SUCCESS; all four applicable workflows green. Independent source/consumer review remains pending; no merge/promotion inferred.\n\n### Exact six-host first-stage ledger\nIDs below have prefix `physical_opening_existence_`. Every case retains `no_authenticated_host_wall_band`; right source primitive unmapped for 81a45c, left unmapped for the other five.\n\n| Physical identity suffix | First source/structural gate | Independently reissued label evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 33d277d4c6b6ce758b0594f9d47ce4d8 | Both candidate flanks painted; no ordinary W4 same-source ancestry/structural identity. Original terminal centre span3.84pt stays below unchanged4pt production gate. | Single870 figure; no area or independently witness-bound second axis. |\n| 81a45c3a33c2a4c0bfdf243aa45a780d | Both candidate flanks painted; right ordinary source membership/structural wall/equivalence unproved. | Single870 figure; no area. |\n| a68d0b7d738b5de9a1588b4e680e1a8f | Both candidate flanks painted; exact W3 short-arm junctions remain AMBIGUOUS/ABSTAINED; no ordinary W4 corroboration or transfer of hosted1215 identity. | Single870 figure; no area. |\n| b248972669988c108ebc90c6ca3908fd | First whole-source flank not solid; separate contained terminal0.24pt remains below existing source gate. | Source label unavailable. |\n| ba7f75a2e5f68bcce87cd00ac1acf90b | First whole-source flank not solid; separate76.8pt contained original terminal still lacks structural role/equivalence/host. | Single870 figure; no area. |\n| f819752382d44a00d9f28feca4b00787 | Both candidate flanks painted; ordinary W4 same-source ancestry and structural identity/equivalence unproved. | Label AMBIGUOUS. |\n\nAll 21 retain exact host/frame/measurement traces. Quantity delivery currently partitions into **8 existing quantities**, **6 host gates**, **3 frame gates on nonquantity objects**, **4 metric-axis/vertical gates on already framed objects**. Physical geometry is independently incomplete: six authenticated hosts lack frames, but **three of those retain valid existing figured-area quantities**. Never revoke those areas or pretend they have complete axis-resolved void geometry.\n\n### Producer lineage handoff for #2297\nThe reader accepts original PDF bytes plus source page selectors; it internally replays original source/host/frame/canonical/quantity producers, re-proves physical source existence and reissues original figured-label evidence. It copies actual producer-issued `snapshot_id`, `decision_scope_id`, physical/host/frame record bodies and existing quantity/measurement IDs. Negative producer traces and attempted selectors remain separate from positive host records. Portable JSON is **UNSIGNED/UNPUBLISHED**, `signed_scope_verified=false`; V1 signatures are unchanged.\n\n- Original PDF SHA `10109b4b6e85e6e27af81f6399ce4b92abfdba80f87dc69dd5887bd6f3a65844`.\n- Actual selected p3 decode root: `source_snapshot_3fcb6bc5c44b51d930e9600080501d27`.\n- Separate all13-pages decoded / p3 topology root: `source_snapshot_7ad8bf09e3ebbec9797df89842574683`.\n- Both use revision `source_revision_31b112fa62447a99d83fe3d10044d2bb`; do not alias the two snapshots.\n- Current selected-root replay independently equals the fresh accepted GitHub archive11929406140 for all21 canonical records, eight complete quantities, full original V1 seal and all8 customer rows. Existing seal fingerprint `ef58f8ae1a963a5b985edfa6dda752f3f338d9d5c42d56969b0e86f538aadfeb`.\n- Exact selected-source quantity/physical/host/measurement packet: [#2297 comment6185049137](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2297#issuecomment-6185049137); GPT3 handoff [comment6185049316](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2004#issuecomment-6185049316); GPT1 [comment6185052239](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2017#issuecomment-6185052239).\n- Independent source/measurement/consumer review and GPT3's versioned signed-consumer contract remain OPEN.\n\n### Separate count and raw-source gates\nOriginal #2765 source workflow38684640994 and full CI SUCCESS; inspected artifact11950095147. Raw group7c32fd8f has a genuinely source-painted contiguous41-cell/9.60pt original endpoint, while the original whole-source41/43 ink failure is retained. This is source-only, not an opening/host/height proof. Raw page closure remains **30 raw /21 resolved /9 unresolved**; count completeness is unproved. No count=1, scope subtraction, physical-nonexistence inference or identity transfer. Two historical native lookalikes retain source-owned opposition and ABSTAIN.\n\nOriginal PDFs, accepted identities/quantities, W3 ambiguity, global2.5pt W2 snap,20,000 input primitive cap, W10 and frozen Full Plan V2 truth/evaluator/denominators/tolerances are unchanged. **Definition of done remains a NEW source-supported physical opening → canonical/measurement → GPT1 quantity → GPT3 independent frozen reconciliation; not achieved by this lineage handoff.**\n\n---\n\n## Historical checkpoints retained below (superseded where they conflict with the checkpoint above)\n\n## Current source-verified checkpoint — 2026-10-12\n\n**Seven raster hosts remain unproven.** Current original production is **21 positive opening hypotheses / 14 authenticated hosts / 9 frames**. The historical two native lookalikes retain complete source-owned dimension/fill opposition and remain ABSTAIN; neither is physical nonexistence proof. Older 23-positive totals and draft/merge references below are historical.\n\nVerified #2454 merged at `4fca39791d3b8d88515802b112f52ce8ee3ed535` after all 24 applicable checks, including original Lot16/Maryborough retention and full source replay. #2477 (`92b593871a2324828b377de7847637739fd79a93`) is implemented and freshly source-replayed, but remains DRAFT pending all applicable CI. W3 already has raw-node-index identities; W4's position lookup overwrote them. New shadow lookup requires unique actual incidence and retains coincident/non-simple chains as negative evidence. Eight abstained chains retain 27 actual fragments; no constructor guard, source cap, physical host or quantity gate is weakened.\n\nAll 81 required associations retain complete W3 spans and experimental membership; 78 have a common candidate address across the full interval. Structural role, raster viewport ownership and physical equivalence remain unproved. Eighteen associations still fail a single-fragment contact predicate. Forty-two W4 candidate addresses remain reused; no alternative is silently overwritten or elected.\n\nFive already-hosted openings still lack complete frames. All 21 width traces need witness topology; all 21 height/schedule/vertical traces lack a contained tag binding. Native and raster universes remain incomplete (125/0 and 30/21 raw/resolved); no count=1 or completeness is inferred. Eight canonical records have figured-area metadata, not a verified bijection to the historical eight sealed quantities.\n\nExact source/canonical identities, receipts, frame/metric/count first gates and independent raw-discovery blockers are committed in documentation-only #2485. #2428 remains blocked: current-base source-positive receipts are equal, but native candidates 125 -> 189 and semantic inventory changes; no comparison is waived. #2420 remains blocked by the actual Maryborough grid-area failure. #2144/#2077 remain preserved until verified integration.\n\nFrozen V2 truth/denominators/evaluator/tolerances, W10 and the 20,000 input cap are unchanged. No new host or accuracy gain claimed.\n\n---\n\n## Historical evidence ledger (retained, superseded by checkpoint above)\n\n## GPT MAX original-source nine-case closure ledger — 2026-10-11\nOriginal **byte-verified** Lot16 PDF: `10109b4b6e85e6e27af81f6399ce4b92abfdba80f87dc69dd5887bd6f3a65844`, page 3. Original production: **23 physical opening claims, 14 authenticated hosts, 9 authenticated frames**; no proof of complete physical opening universe, no benchmark/quantity increase. The distinct nine raw raster candidates (30 registered, 21 individually resolved) are NOT these nine physical opening identities.\n\n### Seven source-backed raster physical existences still unhosted — earlier rejected-component-only evidence\nAll IDs have prefix `physical_opening_existence_`:\n- [ ] `2b2a91e8afaf8b7e9a3e07605a80a4a9` — left source primitive missing, **0** rejected-component run matches its left flank (also 0 on right).\n- [ ] `33d277d4c6b6ce758b0594f9d47ce4d8` — left source primitive missing; **2** original positive-pixel runs: `[581,363]-[585,363]` and `[581,363.5]-[585.5,363.5]`; their actual shadow W2 edges `split_6131` and `split_21591` are both **W3 removed**, neither has a W4 owner. Right side had one *ordinary* authenticated source/W4 candidate. Never copy removed ancestry onto unrelated retained edges.\n- [ ] `81a45c3a33c2a4c0bfdf243aa45a780d` — right source primitive missing, **6** positive pixel-run matches; W2 has both removed and retained source edges; retained W4 alternatives include `wall_ff0035842ff75f2870f6` and branched `wall_bebc0140c3bcb0592875`; local wall identity/whole source band NOT proven.\n- [ ] `a68d0b7d738b5de9a1588b4e680e1a8f` — left source primitive missing, **0** rejected-component run matches its required flank (also zero on right).\n- [ ] `b248972669988c108ebc90c6ca3908fd` — left source primitive missing, **0** rejected-component run matches either flank.\n- [ ] `ba7f75a2e5f68bcce87cd00ac1acf90b` — left source primitive missing, **0** matching positive rejected-component runs on left (eight independent run witnesses exist only on the opposite right flank).\n- [ ] `f819752382d44a00d9f28feca4b00787` — left source primitive missing, **6** positive pixel-run matches; shares vertical original-positive ink and experimental W4 alternatives with `81a45c3a...`; physical association remains ambiguous.\n\n### Two non-raster hostless hypotheses — review opening existence rather than invent hosts\n- [ ] `415d34ddc0c7591b181ddadc11aefe1d`: native candidate geometry `[1011.12,450.72]-[1011.12,442.20]` appears on original drawing's 90/450 **dimension annotations**, not within an authenticated wall aperture. Require complete source-owned dimension component opposition; visual proximity alone must NOT delete original candidate or assign a host.\n- [ ] `b222d5310a7df1d632d5daab1a676645`: native candidate geometry `[821.40,730.80]-[720.12,730.80]` lies on **AREA CALCULATIONS** title table. Original PDF paint command `seqno=1682` is fill-only pale neutral `(0.960784,0.960784,0.960784)`, two rectangles `y721.56..730.80` and `740.04..749.28`, no stroke. Generic strict opposing-fill source proof proposed in draft #2395. Must validate all 6 candidate support ownership and retain old host/frame identities before closing as an opposed false positive.\n\n### Required autonomous engineering gates\n1. Original-source #2356 pixel producer **merged** at `c1953a55e4a54a8f0e0ff7b03d5ca9257f302ef2`, original Lot16 source/retention CI passed. Read-only original detector disposition #2340 **merged** at `d4e135bf8a913e66e3b05452422832ebe63d295a`.\n2. Complete exact-source cross-report pixel/G17/W2/W4 join #2361 (currently draft); the first source run failed because ten actual W2 snap-loss fragments lack source parents; corrected to retain them as **negative** evidence, no borrowing lineage, and derived-fragment inventory size kept separate from 20,000 input primitive safety cap. Re-run gate.\n3. For three missing-source sides with positive runs, prove source wall-role visibility, actual surviving W2 geometry, W3 provenance and unambiguous **local physical W4 ownership**; do not elect first/nearest candidate. For other four, use original/source-positive detector discovery without inventing pixels.\n4. For false native candidates, authenticate complete opposing PDF annotation/table paint-role source and retain raw hypotheses as unresolved; do not claim physical nonexistence from visual inspection.\n5. Before ANY source-producer/host merge require exact original Lot16 14 host and nine frame receipt preservation and Maryborough source parity. Do not merge #2364 if Maryborough grid regression is failing.\n6. No frozen V2 manifest/reference/denominator/evaluator/tolerance modification, no guessed wall, geometry or opening count, no published quantity without source authority and never relax the 20,000 input primitive cap.\n\n## Dependencies\n#2356 (merged), #2340 (merged), #2361 (draft, source audit), #2395 (draft, native neutral-fill source opposition), #2364 (draft, original Maryborough grid regression BLOCKED), rejected source-loss experiments #2032 and #2161 (archived, unmerged).\n\n**Done means every case has an independently source-proven legitimate host OR explicitly evidenced non-opening opposition/ABSTAIN, with the complete old source host/frame identity retained, and re-run exact source/benchmark reconciliation. A mere host count of 23 is NOT completion.**\n\n## Current continuation — original-source audit and draft implementation\n\n**No nine-case closure or recovered-host gain is claimed.** The default original control remains 23 claims / 14 authenticated hosts / nine frames. Frozen V2 truth/evaluator/tolerances/denominators and the 20,000 input-primitive cap are unchanged.\n\n- **#2403**, exact head `76675643bb865048d68f74af021866bb56a718fc`: clean-base native pale-neutral fill opposition plus a separate fresh-PDF retention audit. Original source replay is 23→22 claims solely by opposing the unhosted/unframed Area Calculations hypothesis; all 14 host receipts and nine frame receipts are exactly retained. The default strict comparator is unchanged. Four stale source workflow comparisons were corrected; exact-head job `114456830360` exposed the fourth historical positive-universe equality failure, and the revised workflow now independently replays the exact base and reauthenticates the original opposition. Maryborough still requires exact binding/firm-frame parity. Keep draft pending new exact-head source gates.\n- **#2408**, exact head `f7fedb6da0067291fd9a0257e3130fc886795907`: complete original foreground-to-local W2/W3/W4 audit, independently replayed from immutable PDF bytes. All 14 flanks have positive original ink; 6,016 raster runs + 4,083 ordinary source inputs = **10,099 input primitives**, zero unmapped source parents. Derived inventory: 16,409 W2 edges, 46,270 snap-collapsed fragments, 6,013 W3-retained edges and 4,682 W4 records. One W4 address is reused; all alternatives remain explicit, no owner is elected. Remote surviving ancestry never substitutes for lost local geometry.\n- **#2411**, exact head `0431afb45ab66f295e8550fc8a649b0187be529d`: original native text paint partition audit. The 415d dimension hypothesis spans two chains. Four of six supports already have annotation-component coverage; the two lower-chain supports remain uncovered because original word `90450` has an ABSTAINED text-integrity receipt (`text_trace_unavailable`). Source paint commands 954=`90` and 956=`450` are separated by fill-path 955. The audit retains exact glyph/paint ownership and the negative receipt, never feeds untrusted numeric partitions into the component compiler, and leaves the live hypothesis unchanged. **This case remains open.**\n\n### Complete foreground missing-side local disposition\nThese are original run alternatives, not opening objects or recovered hosts. Identity prefix means `physical_opening_existence_`.\n\n| Identity prefix | Required side | No local W2 survivor | Local W3 discard | Local W4 alternative, authority unproved |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `2b2a91e8` | left | 0 | 3 | 2 |\n| `33d277d4` | left | 7 | 0 | 0 |\n| `81a45c3a` | right | 5 | 0 | 0 |\n| `a68d0b7d` | left | 0 | 5 | 1 |\n| `b2489726` | left | 0 | 3 | 2 |\n| `ba7f75a2` | left | 0 | 5 | 3 |\n| `f8197523` | left | 6 | 0 | 0 |\n\nThus three required sides lack locally surviving W2 geometry; four have local W4 alternatives without original structural wall-role, authenticated floor-plan viewport and physical-equivalence authority. The earlier rejected-component-only evidence above remains historical; this fresh complete-foreground audit supersedes its discovery gaps without promoting a host.\n\n### Validation and next gates\n\n74 focused opposition/strict-retention tests, 107 existing source/opening/frame tests, 60 complete-foreground/local-stage tests, and 152 native partition/dimension/text-integrity tests passed. Original PDF source replays and strict existing-host/frame preservation passed locally. Provider isolation, V2 integrity, Ruff F821/F823 and workflow YAML/inline Python checks passed. Source-opposition smoke passed. Its full local suite: **11,190 passed, 51 skipped, 13 xfailed, one schedule-identity failure**, independently reproduced on unchanged `9dc7125`; this is not a passed full-suite claim or a waiver of CI.\n\nAll three PRs remain draft until required exact-head CI/source checks pass. #2395 remains active and overlaps the generic fill-role delta in #2403; reconcile that overlap before integrating either successor. #2364 remains blocked by its Maryborough grid regression. Next source engineering: prove safe source ownership across the intervening native paint at the existing text authority; recover source-owned local W2 fragments in shadow; prove structural role/viewport/equivalence for the surviving W4 alternatives. Do not borrow lineage, relax tolerances/cap, or close a case solely from an ink/host count.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KAVentures/openworkgraph/issues/326","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KAVentures/openworkgraph","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KAVentures/openworkgraph/issues/326/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KAVentures/openworkgraph/issues/326/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KAVentures/openworkgraph/issues/326/events","html_url":"https://github.com/KAVentures/openworkgraph/issues/326","id":6001055892,"node_id":"I_kwDOUdL9kM8AAAABZbDYlA","number":326,"title":"Roadmap 2: from first slices to competitor-depth process and task intelligence","user":{"login":"KAVentures","id":134240819,"node_id":"U_kgDOCABaMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/134240819?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures","html_url":"https://github.com/KAVentures","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KAVentures/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":559,"created_at":"2026-10-23T15:55:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T05:06:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Why a second roadmap\nEvery item in #264 now has a first implementation in `main`. That is not parity with Mimica, UiPath (Task Mining, Process Mining, Task Capture, Automation Hub, Communications Mining), Celonis, Soroco, Microsoft Power Automate Process Mining, SAP Signavio or Skan.ai. #264's own gate (\"test competitor-style UX against realistic consenting datasets before calling it parity\") has not been met, and most items are breadth, not depth.\n\nThis issue tracks the depth needed for an all-encompassing open-source OWG. It keeps OWG's foundations: local-first capture, consent, evidence/policy/permission separation, agent handoff over MCP, Discovery Mode, and no hidden upload or productivity scoring. It is capability parity, not copying proprietary code, branding or UI.\n\n## Current state vs competitors (honest baseline)\n| Area | Competitors | OWG in `main` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Source connectors | Continuous extraction from SAP, Oracle, Salesforce, ServiceNow, Workday… | CSV (now with chosen extra columns kept as attributes, #366); selected Jira/GitHub/Zendesk/Stripe cases; append newer exports to saved logs (#360) |\n| Scale | Billions of events, columnar engines | Local SQLite; DuckDB event-log workspace with 10M-event acceptance (#327) |\n| Object-centric mining | Linked order/invoice/delivery objects | OCEL 2.0 JSON and XML import/export with per-object-type case notions and literal identities (#327, #331, #338); object-centric maps (#336, #345) |\n| Analytics | Root cause, KPIs, benchmarks, simulation, token-replay conformance | Variants, case evidence, KPIs with cohort filters/exports, benchmarks, what-if simulation, root-cause associations, path and saved-graph alignment conformance with fitness/precision, classic token replay (#328, #330, #332, #333, #335, #339, #350) |\n| Performance and change | Disco/ProM processing vs waiting, dotted chart, Apromore compare and drift | Processing vs waiting time from lifecycle or end-time data (#366), dotted chart (#367), side-by-side map comparison (#368), concept drift change points (#369) |\n| Organizational mining | Handover-of-work and working-together networks, activity/resource views | Pseudonymous handovers, shared cases and activity × resource matrix (#352) |\n| Signals and actions | Celonis Action Engine / UiPath process alerts on KPI thresholds | Saved KPI, case and compliance signal rules with evidence cases and new-since-last-check; signals never act (#355, #358, #362) |\n| Ad-hoc analysis | Celonis PQL, custom analyses | Typed no-SQL analysis builder with saved analyses (#357) |\n| Opportunity pipeline | UiPath Automation Hub idea pipeline and prioritization | Local reviewable pipeline with states, history, ease/impact assessment and quadrants; approval never authorizes execution (#361); scenario calculator and implementation alternatives |\n| Compliance rules | ABBYY Timeline / Signavio adherence / ProM Declare, segregation of duties | Declare-style rules incl. four eyes with violation rates and cases, saveable as signals (#362) |\n| Predictive monitoring | ABBYY Timeline, IBM Process Mining, Celonis predictive | Backtested remaining-time and outcome-risk predictions for open cases (#363) |\n| Map abstraction | Fluxicon Disco / Apromore activity and path sliders, performance overlay | Activity/path sliders with frequency and performance per edge (#364) |\n| Model discovery | Apromore Split Miner, PM4Py inductive miner, Signavio | Inductive-miner style discovery into reviewable catalog drafts with BPMN export (#365) |\n| Task mining | Automatic cross-team task discovery | Candidate workflows; team-level k-anonymous motifs (#348); cross-day resumption (#347); multi-signal linked work items, identifiable-membership reconstruction F1 0.54 → 0.57 (#349) (target 0.90) |\n| Automation runtime | Robots, orchestration, monitoring | Non-executing starters (Codex/Claude/n8n/AI SDK), shadow evaluation, run-report and SDK journal monitoring (#340, #353, #354). Executing robots stays out of scope by design |\n| Documentation | AI-written PDDs with step screenshots | Structural PDD/SDD tables; versioned masked-screenshot PDD packages (#337, #344) |\n| Communications mining | Email/ticket intent mining | Local intent/entity/volume mining of selected exports, aggregates only (#334) |\n| Validation | Years of deployments | No real pilot; A/B/C harness never run on real users |\n\n## A. Task mining and reconstruction quality\n- [x] Reconstruction beyond exact record refs: combine resource refs, tab context, clipboard linkage and app/surface continuity with explicit uncertainty. Never merge by time alone (#349): merges on same record, observed clipboard transfer and single-record tabs; multiplexed/unreferenced tabs and app continuity are unmerged ambiguous candidates.\n- [ ] Meet the preregistered thresholds in `evals/reconstruction` (assignment F1 ≥ 0.90, contamination ≤ 0.05) on the family holdout, without regressing interruption rejection. Note: deterministic signals reach 0.52 identifiable holdout F1 with #349; accepting every ambiguous candidate reaches 0.65 but 0.125 contamination. The rest is semantic linkage, so 0.90 likely needs an LLM-graded linker run with a user-supplied API key.\n- [x] Cross-session and cross-day task continuity (resumed work), with explicit confidence (#347): lease-scoped idle-gap sessions and resumption candidates from shared stable pointers, never time alone.\n- [x] Team-level task discovery from consenting, k-anonymous aggregates (#348): per-team and cross-team motifs, k floor per cell, complete weeks only, non-retroactive team membership, rounding, audited.\n\n## B. Event-log interoperability and scale\n- [x] OCEL 2.0 (object-centric event log) import and export (JSON and XML), with validation and bounded memory (#327, #331, #338).\n- [x] XES import/export for interoperability with PM4Py, ProM, Apromore, Celonis and Signavio (#327).\n- [x] Columnar local analytics engine (DuckDB) for multi-million-event logs, with 10M-event acceptance (#327).\n- [x] Object-centric process maps: object types, per-object lifecycles and inter-object relations (#336, #345).\n- [ ] Enterprise source connectors with real sandbox acceptance: Salesforce, ServiceNow, SAP (export or OData), Microsoft 365/Outlook. Each is opt-in and provider-scoped with incremental extraction. *(open for the agent working on source connectors; #360 provides the append/dedupe path they can load into)*\n\n## C. Analytics depth\n- [x] Token-replay or alignment conformance against reviewed BPMN: fitness, precision, deviating cases. Path alignment (#328), paired parallel models (#329), saved process graph comparison (#335), fitness bounds and precision (#339) and classic produced/consumed/missing/remaining token replay with per-activity diagnostics (#350).\n- [x] Root-cause and influencer analysis: case attributes associated with slow, reworked or deviating cases, with effect sizes and confidence, never causal claims (#328).\n- [x] KPI definitions and dashboards (throughput, wait, rework, SLA breach, automation rate) over saved logs, with filters and exports (#328, #330).\n- [x] What-if simulation of TO-BE designs (arrival rates, durations, resources) with stated assumptions (#332, #343).\n- [x] Benchmarking between cohorts, teams or periods using existing cohort comparison (#330).\n\n## D. Documentation, communications, runtime\n- [x] PDD with optional, consented, redacted step screenshots and an AI-drafted narrative clearly marked as a draft (#337, #344).\n- [x] Communications mining over opted-in email/tickets: intents, entities, volumes, without retaining raw text beyond the existing work-text consent (#334).\n- [x] Deployment monitoring: ingest outcomes from customer-run automations (n8n, AI SDK, Agents SDK) as event logs with success/handoff/failure, step hotspots and period drift (#340).\n\n## E. Proof\n- [ ] Real consenting pilot (2–4 weeks, multiple teams). Grade with `evals/reconstruction`, `evals/product_value.py` (paired McNemar and bootstrap) and source-verified outcomes.\n- [ ] Competitor-style UX review against realistic consenting datasets; record what fails.\n\n## F. Gaps found in the second parity review\n- [x] F1 Organizational mining over saved event logs: handover-of-work and working-together networks, activity × resource matrix and workload counts. Resources are pseudonymous by default; no per-person speed, ranking or performance scoring (#352).\n- [x] F2 KPI signals (Celonis Action Engine / UiPath alert parity): saved, immutable thresholds over event-log KPIs and case conditions, evaluated on demand, producing signals with evidence cases and new-since-last-check. Signals never execute actions (#355, #358).\n- [x] F3 Ad-hoc analysis builder (PQL-like): typed, bounded filter/group/aggregate over event logs without raw SQL, exportable and saveable (#357).\n- [x] F4 Automation opportunity pipeline (Automation Hub parity): reviewable idea → assessing → approved/rejected/on hold → implemented with history and stale-edit refusal, ease questionnaire and impact modeled from stated assumptions, priority quadrants; never claimed savings or execution (#361).\n- [x] F5 Incremental append for saved event logs with duplicate skipping, batch-prefixed IDs, transactional conflict rollback and an append history (#360).\n\n## G. Gaps from other vendors (ABBYY Timeline, Signavio, Disco, Apromore, IBM, PM4Py)\n- [x] G1 Predictive monitoring for open cases: remaining time and outcome risk from comparable historical prefixes, with temporal backtesting, calibration and minimum-support suppression. Predictions are estimates, never commitments or performance ratings (#363).\n- [x] G2 Declarative compliance rules (Declare-style): response, precedence, existence counts, not-co-existence, response-within-time and segregation of duties (four eyes), with violation rates and violating cases, saveable as signals. Descriptive checks, not verified policy or legal compliance (#362).\n- [x] G3 Disco-style process map with activity and path abstraction sliders and a frequency/performance overlay (#364).\n- [x] G4 Automatic process model discovery from a log into a reviewable draft (decisions, loops, structured parallel regions) with BPMN export via the existing catalog (#365).\n\n## H. Performance and change analysis (Disco, ProM, Apromore, Celonis)\n- [x] H1 Processing vs waiting time from start/complete lifecycle events (XES `lifecycle:transition` or a CSV column) or a per-event end-time attribute: per-activity processing and waiting, flow efficiency, waiting hotspots by transition. No per-person speed. CSV import can keep chosen extra columns as event attributes (#366).\n- [x] H2 Dotted chart (Disco/ProM): events over time per case, coloured by activity, with relative or absolute time, sampling and hover (#367).\n- [x] H3 Process map comparison (Apromore compare): two cohorts or periods side by side, with case-share and median-gap differences per path and confidence intervals (#368).\n- [x] H4 Concept drift detection (Apromore/ProM): changes in directly-follows profiles over time windows, with change points from a permutation test, Bonferroni correction and a practical-size floor (#369).\n\n## Acceptance gates (as in #264, plus)\n- Backward-compatible REST/MCP, exports, dashboard, capture and Discovery Mode.\n- Cross-tenant isolation, revocation/retention, safe HTML, semantic ambiguity and concurrent-edit tests.\n- Performance acceptance at the stated scale for every engine change.\n- No derived path or statistical association presented as a verified business workflow, cause or authorization.\n\n## Coordinating parallel agents\nTo avoid collisions, claim an item before starting it (in a comment or by marking it *claimed* here), work on a branch named after the area (e.g. `feat/ocel-import`), and keep shared files (`tests.yml`, `dashboard/index.html`, the process model) to minimal additive edits. Both agents are extending the event-log workspace files (`server/event_log_*.py`, `shared/event_log_formats.py`, `dashboard/event_log_workspace.js`); merge `main` before pushing to them.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KAVentures/openworkgraph/issues/326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KAVentures/openworkgraph/issues/326/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}